{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070799-advice-for-streamlining-larger-combats-with-mages","id":1070799,"title":"Advice for streamlining larger combats with mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T12:38:57-07:00","id":1070799,"title":"Advice for streamlining larger combats with mages","content":"Hello, forum!<br /> <br /> I'm looking for some help in coming up with rule changes to streamline and speed up combats with more than a couple of enemy combatants. I've read &quot;mass combat&quot; posts on this forum already, but I'm not looking for rules to send armies against each other. The sort of situation that I'm referring to is combats with 10-20 mages against either Sleepwalkers or other mages. This situation is going to come up in my game as groups of Apostates (fledgling Nameless Orders, really) are coming under close scrutiny by Seers, and some hostility between Nameless Orders or the Nameless Orders and the Seers themselves seems all but assured. If it matters, the context is that the PCs are Seers inserted into one of the Nameless Orders to scout out the area. My goal here is to make these types of fights fun and dramatic, but also streamlined enough to do anime-esque group combats without it bogging things down too terribly much. <br /> <br /> Some ideas that I've come up with so far are:<br /> <br /> * No initiative rolls. Each faction will go on the highest initiative modifier of their group, going down from highest to lowest. <br /> <br /> * All of an individual group will use the same Defense and Armor value. This will be calculated based on the medium values that the individual members have, most likely. This will not happen to the leaders' stats.<br /> <br /> * The leader of each group automatically gets the Inspiring merit, and is assumed to be using it to give extra dice to half the opposing group's Defenses. <br /> <br /> * Paradox <i>will </i>come up with this many mages. My initial thought of how to handle this was a &quot;group&quot; pool for Paradox, similar to the Magical Buildup hack in Armory Reloaded, and only rolling for new Paradox effects at the end of every so often. Not sure how often.<br /> <br /> Any other suggestions, ways to streamline things, or ways to improve upon my ideas? In particular, any suggestions on handling Paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11494-mischiefmoon","name":"MischiefMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T13:02:20-07:00","id":1070817,"title":"","content":"If there are so many people involved in a fight that it becomes bothersome to keep track of all of them it's probably best to break the combat up into individual sections. In big battles it is usually really hard to keep track of all of the other parts of the battle assuming you're in the middle of it. So have your mages go against groups of similarly numbered enemies while their allies clash with the rest of the forces around them. You can, and I would recommend you do, have outside forces occasionally enter and exit their particular fight, but this makes it a lot easier to handle.<br /> <br /> As an example, say it breaks out into a battle of ~20 allied mages vs a force of ~30 other mages. After whatever opening strike is made have the PCs (assuming 3-5 players here) square off against a similar number of enemies, probably around +-2. While that is happening describe how everyone around them is also squaring off against each other. Then like a turn or 3 (depending on how well your mages are handling themselves) have some AoEs cut through their battle, maybe sectioning them off from the ones they were originally fighting and setting them against a new set of opponents. Or, have another groups fighting briefly spill over into their fight.<br /> <br /> Maybe have some groups handily defeat others and come to reinforce them (if allies) or the enemy (if bad guys). And If you really don't mind splitting the party even have them get separated in the heat of combat. It does make it a bit more complex (running 2 different but still connected combats at once), but it could be pretty cool as they get split up and fight their way through until meeting back up a bit later.<br /> <br /> I'll admit these aren't really rule changes so much as scene framing tools, they still might be of help to you in dealing with the complexities of mass combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:24:53-07:00","id":1070944,"title":"","content":"Down and Dirty combat is a thing that can model it. If you want it a bit more complex than just squaring off rolls, make it team-work, or let some secondary actors counter other secondary actors, or inverse their potential, this is, instead of adding bonus to your side's primary actor, it adds penalties to the other. Narrate each roll appropriately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T17:51:18-07:00","id":1070957,"title":"","content":"I&quot;m sure you already thought of this, but, it cannot be said enough--time magic.<br /> <br /> You need to account for time magic. If your system doesn't make it possible to go back a turn easily, then you need to dissuade any time mages in your player-base from using it in agreement that no enemies will use it either. The more people you have, the more time magic becomes a nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T01:38:29-07:00","id":1071123,"title":"","content":"Use down and dirty combat(spellcasting). Take the highest dice pool of the side and add +1 for every member andccount for some artifacts if you wish. Roll and narrate effect.<br /> I remember that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> had some rules for battles in werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T02:52:49-07:00","id":1071146,"title":"","content":"Prepared <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857534-dark-eras-battle-mass-combat-rules\">Mass Combat rules</a> to use in Dark Eras, mostly Viking Era - but in those times it was more like '50 people on one side, 80-100 on other' in most smaller battles. With that in mind, I think you can use this rules for Mage - you only need to devise more how to resolve Arcana that two sides use in 15 minutes of Battle Turn time. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> advised to use Brief Nightmares for Units, which I approve and will use in newest revision of rules. Maybe I will post newest version just in a second in original topic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The only thing you need to take consider in those is that one Unit should be about of numbers of one cabal if you do not use military personal split. So I would say you make one Unit ( as Brief Nightmare ) per each 5-6 mages or Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-31-2017, 05:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T02:58:01-07:00","id":1071152,"title":"","content":"Also, keep a bottle of gin handy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}